<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zaman Shah Durrani</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Zaman Shah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zaman Shah <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durrani-empire">Durrani</a> was ruler of the Durrani Empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> in the 1790s, a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-shah-abdali">Ahmad Shah Durrani</a>. He launched several invasions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a> note that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a> exploited Zaman Shah's withdrawal from the Punjab in 1799 to seize <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lahore">Lahore</a>, beginning his consolidation of power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zaman-shah-durrani.jpg" alt="Zaman Shah Durrani" width="283" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emperor_Zaman_Shah_Durrani_of_Afghanistan-cropped-2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
